  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Last year, a library had $8,000$ visitors. This year, the number of visitors is $25%$ greater than last year. How many visitors did the library have this year?\n\nThe library had\n{{field-1}}\nvisitors this year.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the number of visitors this year, we apply a $25%$ increase to the previous year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $25%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+25%=125%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n125%=\\frac{125}{100}=1.25\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original number of visitors by $1.25:$\n\n$$\n8,000\\times 1.25=10,000\n$$\n\nSo, the library had $10,000$ visitors this year.",
